prompt Baton ORDER/ABSENCE discipline and recursion-prompts/copal-inner.md's fruit: take one unrostered witness under tools/gen/chapter/, claim it, roster it, prove it from both sides.
think Confirmed a clean tree and the round-open already settled, then re-measured unrostered chapter witnesses by diffing tools/gen/chapter/*_witness.rish against `path` lines in construction/standing-equipment.kyri rather than trusting the prior lap's count.
think Chose ironbeetle_ep032_census_witness.rish, byte-for-byte the same shape as ep001 through ep031 apart from its say-lines and census filename: reads gratitude/ironbeetle (presence-only vendored prose, no git submodule) once, no clone-absent skip leg.
think Proved both legs on metal before claiming: present, the witness reads verdict=ok with all seven named facts yes; moved aside to /tmp and restored, it refuses with the named ABSENT assertion.
think Ran fleet_claim_scan.sh --check first -- commits_behind=0, board clear, one unrelated live claim (bakery-root-finder-convert) with no path overlap -- then opened copal-ironbeetle-ep032-census-roster via fleet_claim.sh --open, which carried construction/ITINERARY.md's Git nib forward on its own.
think First commit attempt was refused twice by the commit-msg mechanism-sentence hook for carrying zero vocabulary words from its named list; rewrote the body naming the file construction/fleet-claims.kyri plainly until it passed.
think Pushed the claim clean on the first try. Added the ironbeetle_ep032_census guard row to standing-equipment.kyri in the ep028/ep030/ep031 shape, re-proved the witness GREEN with the roster edit in place, then closed the claim with fleet_claim.sh --close, which removed the claim record and carried the nib forward again.
think Refreshed readme_metrics and geode_libraries and ran pin_bound_touch_scan.sh before committing the roster -- no diffs, all pins under bound.
think The roster commit's push was rejected once by a peer landing mid-send (incense's sixteenth fallow reading). Rebased, let the post-commit hook's own debt-check fire, re-ran both generated-page refreshes and the pin scan (no diffs again), re-checked the claim board (clear, overlap_mine=1 against my own still-building entry read from stale upstream), amended the nib to the new HEAD^ via remember_git_nib.rish write amend, staged, amended the commit, and pushed clean.
obs The ORDER clause held exactly as written: committing the claim before the build, then holding no commit/edit/pull mid-build, meant the only moving part at push time was the roster commit itself -- one rebase, one re-amend, done.
obs fleet_claim.sh carrying the card on both --open and --close spared two of the three nib edits this lap needed; only the mid-send rebase needed a hand, since it moved HEAD by a means the tool does not watch.
obs The commit-msg hook's mechanism-sentence gate caught a genuinely thin first draft -- the claim commit's own first attempt named no file, function, or path in its body, only prose about what a claim is for.
